# Cancelling reactions, P4.7 (RFC-0084): Cancel is a site, so the body of a When, which runs at
# once when its guard succeeds and cannot suspend, cannot cancel a reaction itself: it hands off
# to a task that does.
var X:i64 = 0
Other:task(void) = When(X > 5, void(0))
Stop:task(void) = When(X > 0, Other.Cancel())
